## 1. The first two operations have different requirements

The source-only A0 preflight requires exactly three independently authenticated selections: `legal_cohort`, `origin_and_decoder`, and `resources_and_cost`. The existing checker verifies that list separately from measured Stage A. A0 uses the reviewed source-only route without optimizer updates. It still requires the selected Source epoch, permitted cohort, decoder provenance, tokenizer/prefill and ordinary local ownership. See the [existing first-run handoff](/tmp/decoder-training-original-parent-retention-private-v01/first-run-handoff.json) and [checker](/tmp/decoder-training-transport-original-scope-private-v01-HGGFq0NH/check_design.py:3208).

The proposed first measured teacher pilot has nine attempts per selected configuration and seed: one source-only arm, four teacher-specific tap-only arms and four relational arms. Compare each relational arm with its own tap-only control, then inspect tap-only versus source-only for instrumentation effects. Preserve all four teachers, common TRAIN membership, complete outputs, checkpoints, observation schedule and paid work. Freeze the registered study, thresholds, seed/checkpoint grid, retention reference and untouched FINAL custody before the measured comparison. This is a teacher-supervision pilot; the broader conditioning and distillation grid remains a later comparison. Nothing here selects either operation.

## 2. Source selection uses the existing paired route

The original Source owner selects the current Datasets and Accelerate physical roots, exact HEAD/tree/index/exclude expectations, approved role list, funded ledger, byte ceilings, namespace and launch window. Preserve every prior charge. The original paired selector must actually close with its ref-stream commitments and terminal evidence before the existing Reader consumes the selected plan. The Reader observes and authenticates both indexes inside that operation. See the [held Reader](/tmp/decoder-training-stage-a-ref-stream-cap-private-v01-5iuVOjcO/reader.py.DATA:265) and [index verification](/tmp/decoder-training-stage-a-ref-stream-cap-private-v01-5iuVOjcO/verify_standalone_git.py:316).

A separate standalone READ1 is an owner sequencing option, not a v4 Reader API prerequisite. If the owner retains that option, price it separately. If the owner chooses the integrated observation, retain all paired opening, closing and Source guards. The user's Source-cap increase authorization persists; the existing owner can apply it with a fresh exact ledger and scope without another generic confirmation. This does not select numerical compute budgets or create a new reader, profile, supervisor or queue.

Guide581 is the last saved decoder handoff boundary, not a current physical allocation. Its Datasets index was 7,070,589 bytes, and its qualified physical Accelerate index was 4,469,929 bytes. Two reads plus their growth sentinels total 11,540,520 bytes, exceeding the historical 6,356,992-byte headroom by 5,183,528 bytes before bodies, reports or other owner overhead. Published, writer and qualified physical Accelerate commits remain distinct. Later Git publications do not rebind physical file metadata, import roles, budget or lease custody. The next current quote belongs to the existing owner.

