Route the retained [LIR-0602 request](/tmp/decoder-training-lir0602-owner-choice-private-v01-rbc6d3du/owner-choice-request.INERT.json) through the existing internal review owner. It needs the original documentary selection and independently bound §7214 finding, or an explicit unresolved disposition. That return feeds the original complete TRAIN and separately reviewed DEVELOPMENT admissions. It does not itself admit either partition. The [joint cohort candidate](/tmp/decoder-training-a0-joint-reviewed-cohort-private-v01-LHY8yMct/descriptor.json) keeps TRAIN, DEVELOPMENT and Source-epoch inputs null. LIR-1701 retains separate opaque FINAL custody.

The original decoder and checkpoint owners select the exact current backend, tokenizer, configuration, assets and pristine origin. The optimized Qwen route also retains its original calibration/import and independent zero-step reload. Qualification of a new candidate or ByteLevel migration remains separate from historical checkpoint identity. Use the existing backend and resource owners; no new model execution is granted by this handoff.

